114.m:
Brahmā said:
The Avighnatīrtha is proclaimed as the destroyer of all obstacles;
I shall recount the event that happened there too; listen with devotion, O Nārada.

Who delighted his mother with charming dances and songs,
and with all desires and playful amusements;
to that Śrī Gaṇeśa, then exceedingly pleased, I take refuge.

119.m:
Brahmā said:
There is also that which is called Somatīrtha, spoken of by the great-souled ones;
by bathing and giving gifts there, one obtains the fruit of drinking soma.

By them, without doubt, comes the alleviation of all diseases;
from them alone comes food, the preservation of all living beings.
Here the medicinal plants, revered by the world, devoid of ego, spoke to me.

Brahmā said:
The gods and the ṛṣis accepted the word, and Soma did as well;
and the medicinal plants also [accepted] that word, and then went to their own abode.
